  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved the best performance so far (acc=0.619, F1=0.610), showing a large gain over the singleprofile multimodal baseline (config_016, acc=0.527). This jump suggests that how multiple profiles are aggregated is a critical design axis. Uncertainty: we have only tested avgpool for aggregation; it is unclear whether a learned transformer aggregation could capture richer inter-profile relationships and further improve performance, or whether simple averaging is already near-optimal. This experiment (config_020) isolates the aggregation choice (transformer vs. avgpool) while holding all other settings constant (pca_n2000, resnet50, multiprofile, concat fusion), directly testing whether the aggregation mechanism is a meaningful lever. Under a limited budget, this is the highest-information next step: it either confirms avgpool sufficiency (reducing search space) or identifies transformer aggregation as a new promising direction to exploit in subsequent experiments."
